payload.prompt:
Execute task 11.2 of the event-forwarding spec: write README.md in f:\dev_python\checkpoint.

Details:
- Record the exact versions. Read them from the real environment (`.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe --version`, `java -version`, `python -m pip freeze`, requirements*.txt, docker-compose.yml). They are: Python 3.13.9, the JDK (17, 21 or 25; 21 installed), PySpark 4.3.x, and the Spark Kafka connector `org.apache.spark:spark-sql-kafka-0-10_2.13:<pyspark version>`. Explain that the connector is resolved at runtime through `spark.jars.packages` in the shared session builder, which needs network access on first use, or can be shipped as a jar. Also record the Kafka client library, the Kafka image (apache/kafka:3.9.1) and the pinned dependencies. Note the Windows HADOOP_HOME/winutils requirement if it is needed.
- Provide copy-pasteable PowerShell commands that work from a fresh clone, all through the venv interpreter:
  - check `java -version`;
  - create the venv with `C:\Users\[REDACTED]\miniconda3\python.exe -m venv .venv`. State that the venv is built from a Python 3.13.9 interpreter, that this path may differ on other machines, and that conda is not used directly. Check that `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe --version` prints 3.13.9;
  - install with `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt`;
  - run tests with `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest`;
  - state that the CLIs and the test fixture set PYSPARK_PYTHON and PYSPARK_DRIVER_PYTHON to the venv python;
  - `docker compose up -d`;
  - topic creation through scripts/create-topics.ps1, stating that the designed-only topics are not created;
  - the Spark job, using the real CLI arguments from event_forwarding/cli_spark.py;
  - the File_Sink_Worker with availableNow, using the real arguments from cli_file_sink_worker.py;
  - tests without Docker;
  - Kafka tests with `pytest -m kafka`;
  - topic inspection through scripts/inspect-topic.ps1;
  - listing the output directories.
- State the shaping limit: a rule can add a column only as a constant field with a fixed string, number or boolean value. Calculated fields and expressions are not supported.
- Explain why each tested component was chosen, and name isolation as the highest priority.
- State the at-least-once semantics with event_id dedup. Do not claim exactly-once.
- Add separate "Built", "Cut" and "Designed only" sections, and a link to docs/ai-log/.

Do not commit. Do not write docs/design.md or docs/ai-log (other agents do those). Keep the README accurate: verify the commands against the code instead of guessing.

